  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": 5,
      "issue_number": 7629,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "Thanks for the issue, @frenzymadness. We're already tracking this work for our next release.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7629#issuecomment-5796892945",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7629",
      "actor_login": "nateprewitt",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-09-23T14:41:07"
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "issue_number": 7620,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "> That sounds dangerous. How many other (more important) chnages landed in master but were not included in main?\n\nDangerous seems a bit alarmist. Both branches existed at the same time for a couple weeks. PRs opened before that window may have merged into the incorrect branch, but this was ~5 years ago. This is the first instance of anyone pointing out an issue and I don't see other branches with the same behavior. If it was a truly a needed change, I'm certain someone would have re-raised it in the proceeding 5 year window.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7620#issuecomment-5701707334",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7620",
      "actor_login": "nateprewitt",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-09-16T17:26:58"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "issue_number": 7620,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "This looks like an issue of merging into the wrong branch. #5410 was opened against `master` not `main` (likely opened before the cutover). I don't have a strong opinion on preserving it. We can look at removing it for the next release.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7620#issuecomment-5626752874",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7620",
      "actor_login": "nateprewitt",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-09-10T23:21:04"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "issue_number": 7611,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "@Shaivarth, this still contains nonsense content. In the future, this will be treated as spam and may result in removing your accounts access to PSF repositories. Please do not post content you have not validated yourself.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7611#issuecomment-5428118658",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7611",
      "actor_login": "nateprewitt",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-08-26T16:35:07"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "issue_number": 7611,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "@Shaivarth 508 is a WebDAV status code, not a standard HTTP Status code. Your LLM has created references to RFC sections that do not exist. Please validate what you're submitting before opening issues.\n\nWe'll take a look at the 102 mapping.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7611#issuecomment-5427693260",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7611",
      "actor_login": "nateprewitt",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-08-26T15:52:41"
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "issue_number": 7610,
      "pr_number": null,
      "type": "MAINTAINER_COMMENT",
      "excerpt": "@btschwertfeger, we have discussed this [here](https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/7012#discussion_r2748329758) previously. The current setup is intended as there are still millions of daily downloads of setuptools that do not support what you're proposing.\n\nWe will get to a point where we are able to remove this in the future but forcing projects to follow a deprecation that's happened in the last 6 months is fairly aggressive for the Python ecosystem. We'll revisit in the future, but it's still not clear why Cyclonedx is not able to disambiguate two fairly concrete specifiers. The SPDX identifier we include is synonymous with the classifier. Breaking users ability to build the package for the sake of simplifying metadata tooling is not something we intend to do immediately.",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7610#issuecomment-5427534997",
      "github_url": "https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/7610",
      "actor_login": "nateprewitt",
      "actor_association": "MEMBER",
      "happened_at": "2026-08-26T15:32:52"
    }
  ],
